"OverallSummary": "Union Capital Company failed to establish, maintain, and enforce a supervisory system and written supervisory procedures reasonably designed to achieve compliance with suitability requirements and Reg BI's Care Obligation regarding recommendations of leveraged and inverse exchange-traded funds and mutual funds (Non-Traditional Funds). The firm's representatives recommended Non-Traditional Funds without a reasonable basis, failing to consider the products' intended daily holding periods. The violations affected multiple customers, including seniors with moderate risk tolerance. One 98-year-old customer suffered a $700 loss after holding a daily-reset fund for 19 days, while four customers collectively suffered $28,237.85 in total net realized losses from 14 positions held between 14 and 407 days. The violations stemmed from systemic failures: 1) The firm had no specific policies or procedures for supervising Non-Traditional Funds; 2) No guidance was provided on whether or when representatives could recommend these products; 3) No training was offered regarding the terms, features, and risks of Non-Traditional Funds; and 4) No supervisory system was established to ensure representatives considered the intended holding periods identified in the products' prospectuses. The firm agreed to pay $28,237.85 in restitution to affected customers and implement remedial measures to address these deficiencies."
